                                        <div class="tab-pane fade active show" id="pills-1" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="Introduction"><p>The School of Foreign Languages is one of the 21 Schools of Studies at IGNOU, established in 2007, with an aim to:<ul>

<li>Offer innovative, flexible and cost-effective foreign language programme for learners from all sections of the society.</li>
<li>Offer programmes based on the specific needs of the learner to create pool of specialized foreign language experts.</li>
<li>Promote communication across borders and countries.</li></ul></p>
<p>In view of the existing demand due to its multiple practical applications, the study of foreign languages is gaining lots of importance in the academic studies, and the demand is growing continuously. The School works in collaboration with other Schools of the University to develop human resources for a number of sectors, like science, technology, humanities, social sciences and commerce.</p>

<p>The globalization of business has led to the demand of specialized foreign language experts. The expertise in foreign languages can be value addition for professionals of different sectors. The School also offers programmes specific to the requirements of organizations like the Indian Army, Navy and Air force.</p></div>

                                        
                                    </div>
                                    <div>
                                        

                                        <div class="tab-pane fade" id="pills-2" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="Aboutus"  ><p align="justify">The School of Foreign Languages (SOFL) is one of the 21 Schools of the Indira Gandhi National Open University. The School has designed and developed various programmes in Open and Distance Learning (ODL) and in Online Learning Mode.</p></div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div>
                                        

                                        <div class="tab-pane fade" id="pills-3" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="History"  ><p>The School of Foreign Languages is one of the 21 Schools of Studies at IGNOU, established in 2007.</p></div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div>
                                        

                                        <div class="tab-pane fade" id="pills-4" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="Director&#39;sMessage"  ><p align="justify">The School of Foreign Languages is one of thefirst in India to offer full fledged academic programmes in various Foreign Languages in the Open and Distance Learning mode. Established in the year 2007, it is one among the eleven new schools of study that were established by IGNOU aiming at diversification and introduction of new domains of study and research providing access to knowledge creation in foreign language studies.<br> 
<br> 
The School has pioneered courses from Elementary level courses upto Doctoral degree programmes. Presently the School of Foreign Languages offers programmes in nine–09 foreign languages including Arabic, French, Russian, Spanish. German, Persian, Mandarin, Japanese and Korean.<br> 
<br> 
Meticulously designed and in sync with the spirit of NEP 2020, all programmes at the SOFL have initiated a brand new phase in the domain of Foreign Language pedagogy that recognizes it as a vital skill component and contributes extensively upskilling the new age learner and prepares for global employability. Our frequent seminars, workshops and conferences and active collaboration with Foreign Universities, International Organizations and embassies have helped us to build and sustain global quality standards in teaching and research.<br> 
<br> 
Masters programmes in major foreign languages offered in the ODL mode have found huge acceptance among professionals who can now fulfill their dreams of completing Advanced degrees along with their professional commitments. Along with the very successful Research degree programme – Ph.D in French & Arabic, the School has contributed to vital knowledge creation in alternative pedagogies of Foreign languages apart from many other subjects of contemporary relevance and interest.<br> 
<br> 
Through its Online programmes as also a robust presence on SWAYAM-IGNOU MOOCs portal of the Ministry of Education, SOFL has reached out to learners even in the Virtual model. Recognizing the need for teacher training programmes, the School offers also a Diploma in Teacher Training for German language professionals.<br> 
<br> 
SOFL has evolved today into a major Centre for the study and research in Foreign languages and has established itself as an important participant in generating employability as well as advanced studies in the domain.<br> 
<br> 
In the coming days, SOFL is planning to  merge as a centre of excellence in the field of foreign language teaching by adopting latest and innovativepedagogy and digital leaning resources.<br> 

<br>
Best wishes to SOFL<br>
<br>
Prof. Mohammad Saleem<br>
<br>
Director, SOFL</p></div>
